--- a/docs/src/gcode/g-code.adoc
+++ b/docs/src/gcode/g-code.adoc
@@ -1900,15 +1900,24 @@ In example S100 with 1.25MM per revolution thread pitch gives a feed of F125.
 
 [source,ngc]
 ----
-G76 P- Z- I- J- R- K- Q- H- E- L- $-
+G76 P- Z- I- J- K- [X-] [D-] [R-] [Q-] [H-] [E-] [L-] [$-]
 ----
 
 .G76 Threading
 image::images/g76-threads_en.svg["G76 Threading",align="center"]
 
-* 'Drive Line' - A line through the initial X position parallel to the Z.
-* 'P-' - The 'thread pitch' in distance per revolution.
-* 'Z-' - The final position of threads. At the end of the cycle the tool will be at this Z position.
+* 'Drive Line' - The line from the initial XZ position to the programmed
+  final XZ position. If 'X-' is omitted, the drive line is parallel to Z at
+  the initial X position, as in earlier versions.
+* 'P-' - The axial Z 'thread pitch' in distance per revolution. For a
+  tapered drive line, LinuxCNC increases the synchronized path lead so the Z
+  component of motion per spindle revolution remains 'P-'.
+* 'Z-' - The final Z position of the thread drive line. At the end of the
+  cycle the tool will be at this Z position.
+* 'X-' - Optional final X coordinate of the thread drive line. It is a normal
+  axis endpoint, interpreted according to the active G90/G91 distance mode
+  and G7/G8 lathe mode. It is not a taper amount or angle. If omitted, the
+  final X coordinate is the initial X coordinate.
 
 [NOTE]
 When G7 'Lathe Diameter Mode' is in force the values for 'I', 'J' and 'K' are diameter measurements.
@@ -1937,7 +1946,17 @@ Unnecessarily high degression values will produce an unnecessarily high number o
 
 * 'Q-' - The 'compound slide angle' is the angle (in degrees) describing to what extent successive passes should be offset along the drive line.
   This is used to cause one side of the tool to remove more material than the other.
-  A positive 'Q' value causes the leading edge of the tool to cut more heavily.  Typical values are 29, 29.5 or 30.
+  A positive 'Q' value causes the leading edge of the tool to cut more heavily
+  on the first pass. Typical values are 29, 29.5 or 30. 'Q0' keeps every pass
+  on the centered final thread line.
+* 'D-' - Selects the compound-infeed mode. 'D0' (the default) uses the
+  existing fixed compound-infeed direction, with the side selected by the
+  sign of Q. 'D1' alternates
+  roughing passes across the centered final thread line, starting on the flank
+  selected by the sign of Q. The alternating offset decreases with remaining
+  cut depth. The full-depth pass and all H spring passes use the centered final
+  path. Program G96 and its D spindle-speed limit in a separate block from a
+  G76 D infeed selection.
 * 'H-' - The number of 'spring passes'.
   Spring passes are additional passes at full thread depth.
   If no additional passes are desired, program 'H0'.
@@ -1957,8 +1976,10 @@ Thread entries and exits can be programmed tapered with the 'E' and 'L' values.
   cut depth then synchronize and begin the cut.
 
 The tool is moved to the initial X and Z positions prior to issuing
-the G76. The X position is the 'drive line' and the Z position is the
-start of the threads.
+the G76. This position is the start of the 'drive line' and the start of
+the threads. When an X endpoint is programmed, every threading pass,
+including spring passes, follows a line parallel to the tapered drive line.
+Compound infeed offsets and E entry/exit distances follow the drive line.
 
 The tool will pause briefly for synchronization before each threading
 pass, so a relief groove will be required at the entry unless the
@@ -1981,7 +2002,9 @@ from the hole.
 It is an error if:
 
 * The active plane is not the ZX plane.
-* Other axis words, such as X- or Y-, are specified.
+* A Y- word is specified, or another axis besides X or Z is moved.
+* A 'D-' infeed mode other than 0 or 1 is specified.
+* 'G96' and 'G76' use 'D-' in the same block.
 * The 'R-' degression value is less than 1.0.
 * All the required words are not specified.
 * 'P-', 'J-', 'K-' or 'H-' is negative.
